Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:54:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] Round 7: Precompute Gibbs term factors and power-table
 indices

Build compile-time term tables holding the power-table indices of y^J,
y^(J-1) and y^(J-2) and the products n*J and n*J*(J-1), and keep
positive and negative powers in one table. The inner loop loses its
integer-to-float conversions, run-time products and exponent branches.
The ideal-gas part uses the same scheme. The products and summation
order are unchanged, so results are bit-identical.

Workload: domain (48 candidates at 950 K), matrix API both sides.
Official 11-sample run: 0.172 ms -> 0.135 ms, 1.28x (paired 1.33x).
41-sample confirmation: 0.169 ms -> 0.125 ms, paired 1.36x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
